hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"30","On the sutrah in prayer. Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us that he heard Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying toward a man, and ordered him to repeat the prayer. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have completed the prayer. He said: You prayed while looking at him, facing him."
"31","Umar ibn Hafs al-Wassabi narrated to us, Ibn Himyar - meaning Muhammad - narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Jabalah, from Khayr ibn Nu'aym, from Ibn al-Hajjaj al-Ta'i, in a marfu' report, who said: He forbade two men conversing while someone praying is between them. Abu Dawud said: He is Khayr ibn Nu'aym, who was a judge in Egypt."
